.TH DRAFTLING 1 "" "draftling @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
draftling \- distraction-free Markdown, Fountain and plain-text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B draftling
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B draftling
is the editor of the Draftling writing devices as a Linux program. It
runs in a Wayland or X11 window, or full screen on the Linux
framebuffer console, and is used with the keyboard: F1 opens the menu,
F10 the help. Documents are kept in projects (folders) in the data
folder; each project can be synchronised with a Git repository
(Ctrl+G), configured in the project's \fBgit.cfg\fR file or with a
Draftbox password.
.PP
The keyboard layout is chosen in Draftling (Ctrl+L, F1 \-> Settings \->
Keyboard), not by the desktop: keys are read as physical keys of a US
keyboard. Programs named \fBdraftling-\fIpack\fR are the same editor
with another language pack (keyboard layouts, input methods and fonts).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
Documents folder, the device's SD card. Default
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/draftling\fR (\fI~/.local/share/draftling\fR).
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
Settings folder. Default \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/draftling\fR
(\fI~/.config/draftling\fR). Only one Draftling runs per settings folder.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-io\fR \fINAME\fR
Display and input to use: \fBwayland\fR, \fBx11\fR or \fBfbdev\fR (as
far as compiled in; \fB\-\-version\fR lists them). Without it, the
first of them that works is used, in that order.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fbdev\fR \fIDEVICE\fR
Framebuffer device for \fB\-\-io fbdev\fR (default \fI/dev/fb0\fR).
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-geometry\fR \fIW\fBx\fIH\fR
Initial window size.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More messages on standard error; twice for debugging messages.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Errors only.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show the version, the language pack and the I/O backends, and exit.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show the options and exit.
.SH FRAMEBUFFER CONSOLE
With \fB\-\-io fbdev\fR the user needs write access to the framebuffer
(the \fBvideo\fR group) and read access to \fI/dev/input/event*\fR (the
\fBinput\fR group). Started on a virtual console, Draftling switches
the console's keyboard off while it runs, so typing does not reach the
shell; switching consoles is not possible meanwhile.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/draftling/
Projects, documents, \fIwifi.cfg\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/draftling/settings.nvs
Settings (font size, theme, layouts, ...).
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM, SIGINT and SIGHUP save every open document and end the
program; so does closing the window. SIGUSR1 writes the current
screen to \fIscreenshot.ppm\fR in the settings folder.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://draftling.art/, https://github.com/clackups/draftling
